> Both shades and gelatinous cubes are sleep resistant,
> so the paralyze attack had no effect on either one.

Paralysis and sleep are different things with separate resistances.  No
NPC has paralysis resistance ("free action") in nethack.

Note that neither monster has a long lasting paralysis attack; floating
eyes are the exception, not the rule.  Shades have no passive attack, and
the passive attack of a gelatinous cube lasts only 1d4 turns.  Both
active paralysis attacks last for 1d10 turns.

So the OP was probably just seeing the monsters hit each other for
effect, recover, and do it again.  Also, even if the cube *is* paralysed,
that doesn't disable its passive attack.

Perhaps multiple shades (they only appear on a special level, where six
of them are preset) were pounding on a single cube.

